{
  "summary": "Apple stopped populating the legacy US‑GAAP 'Revenues' XBRL concept after its 2018 fiscal year because it adopted the new revenue‑recognition standard ASC 606 (Revenue from Contracts with Customers) effective for fiscal years beginning after December 15, 2017. From FY 2019 onward Apple reports its revenue under the newer concept 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax', so the older 'Revenues' concept has no further facts in the EDGAR XBRL feed.",
  "claims": [
    "The last XBRL fact for Apple (CIK 320193) with concept='Revenues' has fiscal_year=2018 and period_end=2018-09-29, with a reported value of $265,595,000,000.",
    "Starting with fiscal_year=2019, Apple's revenue facts appear only under concept='RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax' (e.g., FY 2019 value $260,174,000,000).",
    "ASC 606 became effective for public companies for annual periods beginning after December 15, 2017, which corresponds to Apple’s FY 2018, prompting the switch from the legacy 'Revenues' concept to the new revenue‑recognition concept."
  ]
}
